(2027266, 278092, 25655, '<td valign="top">A very nice portrait and edit.<br/>However, you shouldn''t have used the yellow background.<br/>Yellow is the first color the human eye will notice. (assuming we are not talking about the color-blind)<br/>Thus the eye will be drawn to the background rather then to your subject.<br/>Unless the background IS your subject.<br/> <br/>For me this is a very good photo but do not meet the challenge.</td>', 'A very nice portrait and edit.However, you shouldn''t have used the yellow background.Yellow is the first color the human eye will notice. (assuming we are not talking about the color-blind)Thus the eye will be drawn to the background rather then to your subject.Unless the background IS your subject. For me this is a very good photo but do not meet the challenge.', '2006-01-11 16:34:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2027282, 277636, 25655, '<td valign="top">First - the blur effect is horrible. Maybe your photo was good, but you have edited it into something bad.<br/>Second - The challenge say "Use a colorful impact to offset your subject from the rest of the photograph". What is your subject, and what is the rest of your photograph exactly? Is your subject the pink flower in the middle? the yellow flowers on the top? There is nothing that draws my eye except for the sloppy blur. For me this is not meeting the challenge.</td>', 'First - the blur effect is horrible. Maybe your photo was good, but you have edited it into something bad.Second - The challenge say "Use a colorful impact to offset your subject from the rest of the photograph". What is your subject, and what is the rest of your photograph exactly? Is your subject the pink flower in the middle? the yellow flowers on the top? There is nothing that draws my eye except for the sloppy blur. For me this is not meeting the challenge.', '2006-01-11 16:40:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2027286, 278433, 25655, '<td valign="top">I love your composition and the use of the primary colors. However, you could have get a stronger impact if the cup would be red and the background blue.<br/>Red is a color that the human eye is drawn to before everything else. (well, yellow comes first. Red comes second)</td>', 'I love your composition and the use of the primary colors. However, you could have get a stronger impact if the cup would be red and the background blue.Red is a color that the human eye is drawn to before everything else. (well, yellow comes first. Red comes second)', '2006-01-11 16:42:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2027292, 277444, 25655, '<td valign="top">Nice night view, but does not meet the challenge at all.<br/>I don''t see anything colorful that offsets your subject from the rest of the photograph. The entire photo is more or less using the same tones. The only things that are colorful are the lights on the distance - top right and top left of the image. And those are definately not the subject of your photo.</td>', 'Nice night view, but does not meet the challenge at all.I don''t see anything colorful that offsets your subject from the rest of the photograph. The entire photo is more or less using the same tones. The only things that are colorful are the lights on the distance - top right and top left of the image. And those are definately not the subject of your photo.', '2006-01-11 16:45:24.000000', NULL, 1),
