(2033909, 277782, 15810, '<td valign="top">The harsh shadow behind your little model makes your shot look like a cheap instant camera flash shot. Shame because everything else about the shot should work extremely well. Even bouncing the flash off a wall or ceiling will help if thats possible.</td>', 'The harsh shadow behind your little model makes your shot look like a cheap instant camera flash shot. Shame because everything else about the shot should work extremely well. Even bouncing the flash off a wall or ceiling will help if thats possible.', '2006-01-13 17:49:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2033914, 278385, 20235, '<td valign="top">Nice use of selective desat here. IMHO I think you could have made the shot tighter to weight the person heavier in the composition. This may have increased the impact of the umbrella. If in full color, your current composition would be perfect. But with the selective desaturation, I don''t think as much of the landscape is needed in order to make an impact here.</td>', 'Nice use of selective desat here. IMHO I think you could have made the shot tighter to weight the person heavier in the composition. This may have increased the impact of the umbrella. If in full color, your current composition would be perfect. But with the selective desaturation, I don''t think as much of the landscape is needed in order to make an impact here.', '2006-01-13 17:54:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2033973, 278198, 20235, '<td valign="top">I really like this still life and the way you''ve composed the elements in the photo. IMHO the top of the palette looks a tad soft/out of focus. And the lighting appears a little on the warm/incandescent side with some shadow casting. Maybe trying alternate WB settings or more neautral lighting would have helped? Just my own opinion, nice shot nonetheless</td>', 'I really like this still life and the way you''ve composed the elements in the photo. IMHO the top of the palette looks a tad soft/out of focus. And the lighting appears a little on the warm/incandescent side with some shadow casting. Maybe trying alternate WB settings or more neautral lighting would have helped? Just my own opinion, nice shot nonetheless', '2006-01-13 18:15:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2033980, 278471, 20235, '<td valign="top">I like the different elements in this shot and how the different colored chairs create visual layers. One thing that distracts me is the apparent fringing/bleeding around some areas of the shot? It is particularly evident around the edges of the blue chairs. Not sure if this was due to post processing?</td>', 'I like the different elements in this shot and how the different colored chairs create visual layers. One thing that distracts me is the apparent fringing/bleeding around some areas of the shot? It is particularly evident around the edges of the blue chairs. Not sure if this was due to post processing?', '2006-01-13 18:19:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2033990, 278168, 20235, '<td valign="top">I really like your decision to tilt the framing in this shot. The color saturation and detail are great..... 8</td>', 'I really like your decision to tilt the framing in this shot. The color saturation and detail are great..... 8', '2006-01-13 18:24:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2033991, 278540, 20235, '<td valign="top">Very nice portrait. Good focus on the eyes and face. The shot seems cropped a little tight IMHO and her face seems a bit ''crowded''? Just my own opinion, nice shot nonetheless.... 7</td>', 'Very nice portrait. Good focus on the eyes and face. The shot seems cropped a little tight IMHO and her face seems a bit ''crowded''? Just my own opinion, nice shot nonetheless.... 7', '2006-01-13 18:26:27.000000', NULL, 1),
