(2044360, 276371, 40667, '<td valign="top">Wow, I can''t belive how amazing dipressed you look in this! lol, it''s amazing, only i really hope you weren''t that dipressed! Wow, i just can''t belive it. In general i really like the position, your eyes look amazing in this! like i mean really! I''m looking at it, and just, really, your eyes make the pic!@ honestly! nice job, and your eyes! lol</td>', 'Wow, I can''t belive how amazing dipressed you look in this! lol, it''s amazing, only i really hope you weren''t that dipressed! Wow, i just can''t belive it. In general i really like the position, your eyes look amazing in this! like i mean really! I''m looking at it, and just, really, your eyes make the pic!@ honestly! nice job, and your eyes! lol', '2006-01-16 17:43:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2044367, 277481, 49007, '<td valign="top">**** Greeting from the Critique Club ****<br/> <br/>First impression: the image is dark.<br/> <br/>Challenge<br/>- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes<br/>- Is subject unique (vs. unoriginal or rehashed)? Yes<br/> <br/>Compostion<br/>- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? There is a lot of dead space to the top and to the left due to the darkness of the image. Crop them out making the starburst more dominant in the image. I wondering if your point was to make the light secondary to the gold ball as it seems to being the point in focus.<br/>- Good use of Depth of Field? Yes. Good Bokeh.<br/>- Good focus? No. The focus is on the gold ball and not on the "Burst of Color" although with this particular subject it''s going to be difficult to get the lights (a light? which one to choose?) in focus.<br/> <br/>Lighting <br/>- Good use of light? As I mentioned earlier, the image is dark, so no. The star filter helps to distribute some light to other parts of the image, but most people are going to think this image too gimicky for it''s use.<br/> <br/>Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:<br/>- Colors and Contrast. I love the colors, especially the out-of-focus yellows, blues, and greens.<br/>- What is my reaction or feelings? If I use my hands to crop the image. It''s amazing, but as submitted it doesn''t excite me.</td>', '**** Greeting from the Critique Club **** First impression: the image is dark. Challenge- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes- Is subject unique (vs. unoriginal or rehashed)? Yes Compostion- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? There is a lot of dead space to the top and to the left due to the darkness of the image. Crop them out making the starburst more dominant in the image. I wondering if your point was to make the light secondary to the gold ball as it seems to being the point in focus.- Good use of Depth of Field? Yes. Good Bokeh.- Good focus? No. The focus is on the gold ball and not on the "Burst of Color" although with this particular subject it''s going to be difficult to get the lights (a light? which one to choose?) in focus. Lighting - Good use of light? As I mentioned earlier, the image is dark, so no. The star filter helps to distribute some light to other parts of the image, but most people are going to think this image too gimicky for it''s use. Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:- Colors and Contrast. I love the colors, especially the out-of-focus yellows, blues, and greens.- What is my reaction or feelings? If I use my hands to crop the image. It''s amazing, but as submitted it doesn''t excite me.', '2006-01-16 17:44:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2044434, 276371, 48717, '<td valign="top">How are you the same girl as in dots &amp; lines?  I never read your comments on that one, and assumed it was a model.  You are MOST VERSITILE!  For you and your portraits, I think it IS "All in the Eyes".  They make you look so very different in each picture you take.</td>', 'How are you the same girl as in dots & lines?  I never read your comments on that one, and assumed it was a model.  You are MOST VERSITILE!  For you and your portraits, I think it IS "All in the Eyes".  They make you look so very different in each picture you take.', '2006-01-16 17:56:41.000000', NULL, 0),
