(2046147, 278533, 43115, '<td valign="top">Followup comment after reading your "photographer''s notes"...<br/> <br/>I suspected the ''noise'' I saw was from USM, and your notes indicate you used it.  You''ve got to be really careful around here with USM to make sure you don''t make edges glow, or else people like me get cranky. :)<br/> <br/>Whenever I apply USM (and I tend to only use it on one out of four photos) I always preview at around 400-600 percent zoom, on a very high contrast edge (where one color shifts abruptly to another one) like the yellow edges of your photo.  That''s where you''ll see the ''glow'' first, and you''ll be best off to back off the USM a smidge when it shows up.<br/> <br/>Your photo was just EVER SO SLIGHTLY over sharpened, but eagle eyed sharpening police like me look out for that stuff. :)<br/> <br/>Congrats on your personal best.  :)  Hope to see more of your stuff in 2006.</td>', 'Followup comment after reading your "photographer''s notes"... I suspected the ''noise'' I saw was from USM, and your notes indicate you used it.  You''ve got to be really careful around here with USM to make sure you don''t make edges glow, or else people like me get cranky. :) Whenever I apply USM (and I tend to only use it on one out of four photos) I always preview at around 400-600 percent zoom, on a very high contrast edge (where one color shifts abruptly to another one) like the yellow edges of your photo.  That''s where you''ll see the ''glow'' first, and you''ll be best off to back off the USM a smidge when it shows up. Your photo was just EVER SO SLIGHTLY over sharpened, but eagle eyed sharpening police like me look out for that stuff. :) Congrats on your personal best.  :)  Hope to see more of your stuff in 2006.', '2006-01-17 00:40:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2046159, 277893, 37893, '<td valign="top">I love the colors and contrast of this image. However, the flowers , to me, are too centered. If they were offset to the right or left I think this would have made for a stronger image. Either way, it''s still a wonderful shot. Great DOF Jeff.</td>', 'I love the colors and contrast of this image. However, the flowers , to me, are too centered. If they were offset to the right or left I think this would have made for a stronger image. Either way, it''s still a wonderful shot. Great DOF Jeff.', '2006-01-17 00:44:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2046287, 276709, 5112, '<td valign="top">Thank you all!</td>', 'Thank you all!', '2006-01-17 01:26:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2046341, 276755, 42013, '<td valign="top">Congrats! You are my first critique club effort. Hope I can give you something worthwhile.<br/> <br/>First impression: I''m first grabbed by the white part of the bulb and then spurred by the title to turn my attention to the filament.<br/> <br/>Composition: You have done a good job of composing the shot, especially the way that the circle shape is repeated(your fingers, the bulb, the filter).  I like your cropping choice.<br/> <br/>Lighting: The lighting was likely tough to control but you have done a good job with it. My only critical comment is that I wish the filament could have popped a little more.  I''m not sure what would have accomplished this but I feel it would have strengthened the image.  I do love the way the light highlites the inside of the filter and the edges of your hand.  This too me is the strongest part of the image.<br/> <br/>Post Processing: This may be inaccurate, but it appears that you thought out your shot very well prior to shutter release which means that PP was minimal. (I haven''t seen your picture details).  Colors look good, sharpness is good.<br/> <br/>Challenge interp: Very subjective, subjects were all over the board and this is where you may have fallen some in the view of the voters. Some of the pics, especially the top 10 were very vivid with their colors. Its hard to figure the voters out :).  But I do agree with the other commenters, this is original and different.  For that I say kudos.<br/> <br/>P.S. I''d love to get some feedback on this critique.  HOpe it gave you something to toss around in your mind.<br/> <br/>Mark</td>', 'Congrats! You are my first critique club effort. Hope I can give you something worthwhile. First impression: I''m first grabbed by the white part of the bulb and then spurred by the title to turn my attention to the filament. Composition: You have done a good job of composing the shot, especially the way that the circle shape is repeated(your fingers, the bulb, the filter).  I like your cropping choice. Lighting: The lighting was likely tough to control but you have done a good job with it. My only critical comment is that I wish the filament could have popped a little more.  I''m not sure what would have accomplished this but I feel it would have strengthened the image.  I do love the way the light highlites the inside of the filter and the edges of your hand.  This too me is the strongest part of the image. Post Processing: This may be inaccurate, but it appears that you thought out your shot very well prior to shutter release which means that PP was minimal. (I haven''t seen your picture details).  Colors look good, sharpness is good. Challenge interp: Very subjective, subjects were all over the board and this is where you may have fallen some in the view of the voters. Some of the pics, especially the top 10 were very vivid with their colors. Its hard to figure the voters out :).  But I do agree with the other commenters, this is original and different.  For that I say kudos. P.S. I''d love to get some feedback on this critique.  HOpe it gave you something to toss around in your mind. Mark', '2006-01-17 01:38:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2046431, 277156, 22479, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the kind comments, everyone! The results exceeded my expectations and I am really glad it was well received.</td>', 'Thanks for the kind comments, everyone! The results exceeded my expectations and I am really glad it was well received.', '2006-01-17 02:03:53.000000', NULL, 0),
