(2046791, 278226, 47717, '<td valign="top">I really like the picture itself, but what makes this a GREAT picture to me is your choice of title.  It takes the imagination to the next level and makes the picture infinitley more interesting.  Perfect title.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-17 05:23:31.</i></td>', 'I really like the picture itself, but what makes this a GREAT picture to me is your choice of title.  It takes the imagination to the next level and makes the picture infinitley more interesting.  Perfect title.', '2006-01-17 05:22:07.000000', '2006-01-17 05:23:31.000000', 0),
(2046825, 275229, 34938, '<td valign="top">I agree with loriprophoto and all of the other post challenge suggestions. To me, it looks like the focus is on the right, and the red flower beind somewhat out of focus. I don''t know about you, but after scoring hundreds of photos, a flower photo has to really be outstanding to get any attention from me, as are many sunsets and landscapes. <br/> <br/>While this is a nice shot, it doesn''t overwhelm you with a WOW!<br/> <br/>I wouldn''t give up though. In the month that I have been in dpc challenges, photos of mine I thought would do really well, don''t seem to, and others, surprise me. I guess when there are 50 flower photos to compete with, the one that ended up getting the blue ribbon deserved it. <br/> <br/>We have to persist, eventually things turn around.</td>', 'I agree with loriprophoto and all of the other post challenge suggestions. To me, it looks like the focus is on the right, and the red flower beind somewhat out of focus. I don''t know about you, but after scoring hundreds of photos, a flower photo has to really be outstanding to get any attention from me, as are many sunsets and landscapes.  While this is a nice shot, it doesn''t overwhelm you with a WOW! I wouldn''t give up though. In the month that I have been in dpc challenges, photos of mine I thought would do really well, don''t seem to, and others, surprise me. I guess when there are 50 flower photos to compete with, the one that ended up getting the blue ribbon deserved it.  We have to persist, eventually things turn around.', '2006-01-17 05:48:25.000000', NULL, 0),
