(2050256, 278541, 51552, '<td valign="top">hey man, i don''t mean to undermine all of your comments, but this would''ve been much better if it weren''t a jeep advertisement.</td>', 'hey man, i don''t mean to undermine all of your comments, but this would''ve been much better if it weren''t a jeep advertisement.', '2006-01-17 20:12:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2050438, 278541, 6349, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by theMilkMan:</b></div><hr/><i> hey man, i don''t mean to undermine all of your comments, but this would''ve been much better if it weren''t a jeep advertisement. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Do you honestly think it would be a better photo without the jeep in it?  I highly disagree.  Perhaps if there was something else at that focal spot to take its place like a person but the Jeep really fits this scene and it has a personality in a way because of the facelike grill and that the vehicle was very much a part of the offroad adventure.  In a way I felt as if people would connect more with the Jeep than they would with a person. (although I do have a few person shots from this area that I mean to upload soon)</td>', 'Originally posted by theMilkMan: hey man, i don''t mean to undermine all of your comments, but this would''ve been much better if it weren''t a jeep advertisement.   Do you honestly think it would be a better photo without the jeep in it?  I highly disagree.  Perhaps if there was something else at that focal spot to take its place like a person but the Jeep really fits this scene and it has a personality in a way because of the facelike grill and that the vehicle was very much a part of the offroad adventure.  In a way I felt as if people would connect more with the Jeep than they would with a person. (although I do have a few person shots from this area that I mean to upload soon)', '2006-01-17 21:02:00.000000', NULL, 0),
