(2052989, 278541, 6349, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by theMilkMan:</b></div><hr/><i> YES I DO THINK IT WOULD BE A BETTER PHOTO WITHOUT THE JEEP IN IT. WITH THE JEEP IN IT, THE IMAGE BECOMES AN ADVERTISEMENT, AND HAS THE AURA OF THE ADS YOU SEE FOR JEEPS IN MAGAZINES. YOU THINK YOUR IMAGE IS BETTER WITH THE JEEP IN IT BECAUSE YOU''VE SEEN PROFESSIONAL SHOTS IN ADVERTISEMENTS AND ON TELEVISION THAT LOOK EXACTLY LIKE THE ONE ABOVE. ALSO, I FEEL THAT A PERSON WHO WOULD CONNECT MORE WITH A JEEP THAN THEY WOULD A PERSON TO BE AN EXTREMELY SHALLOW PERSON. but whatever you''re into. you seem to know what people will vote up, and i guess i''m the only one who has a problem with what this image represents. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No need to yell.  My point was only that from a photographic point of view I felt as if the shot needed a focal spot (the jeep).  I admitted that a person would have worked as well.  I feel as if the photograph would have been empty without something there.  I understand that you are against advertisement.  I enjoyed my time in the jeep and had no problem portraying that.  I don''t personally sell jeeps but I don''t have a problem with anyone that does.  Sorry to upset you.</td>', 'Originally posted by theMilkMan: YES I DO THINK IT WOULD BE A BETTER PHOTO WITHOUT THE JEEP IN IT. WITH THE JEEP IN IT, THE IMAGE BECOMES AN ADVERTISEMENT, AND HAS THE AURA OF THE ADS YOU SEE FOR JEEPS IN MAGAZINES. YOU THINK YOUR IMAGE IS BETTER WITH THE JEEP IN IT BECAUSE YOU''VE SEEN PROFESSIONAL SHOTS IN ADVERTISEMENTS AND ON TELEVISION THAT LOOK EXACTLY LIKE THE ONE ABOVE. ALSO, I FEEL THAT A PERSON WHO WOULD CONNECT MORE WITH A JEEP THAN THEY WOULD A PERSON TO BE AN EXTREMELY SHALLOW PERSON. but whatever you''re into. you seem to know what people will vote up, and i guess i''m the only one who has a problem with what this image represents.   No need to yell.  My point was only that from a photographic point of view I felt as if the shot needed a focal spot (the jeep).  I admitted that a person would have worked as well.  I feel as if the photograph would have been empty without something there.  I understand that you are against advertisement.  I enjoyed my time in the jeep and had no problem portraying that.  I don''t personally sell jeeps but I don''t have a problem with anyone that does.  Sorry to upset you.', '2006-01-18 07:46:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2053108, 277636, 27812, '<td valign="top">Sorry it did not do better, as always simply a pleasent shot... awesome use of DOF, great colors!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-18 08:26:34.</i></td>', 'Sorry it did not do better, as always simply a pleasent shot... awesome use of DOF, great colors!', '2006-01-18 08:26:05.000000', '2006-01-18 08:26:34.000000', 0),
(2053258, 277156, 34192, '<td valign="top">I knew this would place well.  Extremely well taken and edited.  You''ve somehow managed both softness and sharpness together with just enough texture to make the image sing.  Comp and POV are excellent as is toning.  Well done and congrats!</td>', 'I knew this would place well.  Extremely well taken and edited.  You''ve somehow managed both softness and sharpness together with just enough texture to make the image sing.  Comp and POV are excellent as is toning.  Well done and congrats!', '2006-01-18 09:01:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2053685, 276709, 42392, '<td valign="top">this is just "mavalus"-to me this is just perfection-gotta add this and you to my fav''s.also i see that this did not get a one vote on it-did get a 2 and some 3 votes-i gave it a 10 -i don''t understand the low votes i guess i am a long way off from an art critic-thanks again for sharing such a lovely view.</td>', 'this is just "mavalus"-to me this is just perfection-gotta add this and you to my fav''s.also i see that this did not get a one vote on it-did get a 2 and some 3 votes-i gave it a 10 -i don''t understand the low votes i guess i am a long way off from an art critic-thanks again for sharing such a lovely view.', '2006-01-18 10:35:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2053700, 278227, 32321, '<td valign="top">Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>First Impression: Eye drawn to the bright green leaves, then moves over to the right corner, down and then back to the leaves.<br/> <br/>Composition: Good placement of the green leaves, and an effective background. Nice contrast. After looking at it a little longer, my eye keeps getting drawn to the dark spot just right of the plant. Looks like an eye. My mind is trying to see a head in the bark!<br/> <br/>Subject: Think you met the challenge well. <br/> <br/>Technical: Picture lacks sharpness. As if the focus is off. The leaves need to be more crisp. They look flat. Color is there, but not the plant detail. DOF looks good. This could be as a result of  the ISO:400, or the file size you submitted. Reviewing your file size, I see you didnt take advantage of the 640 max dimension, and your file size was well below the 150k allowed. (624 X 437, 115k)<br/> <br/>Summary: Nice picture! Good eye and kudos for having your camera handy! I think you captured the theme well. Good burst of color on a grey/black background! Better detail on the green leaves would have helped.<br/></td>', 'Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club. First Impression: Eye drawn to the bright green leaves, then moves over to the right corner, down and then back to the leaves. Composition: Good placement of the green leaves, and an effective background. Nice contrast. After looking at it a little longer, my eye keeps getting drawn to the dark spot just right of the plant. Looks like an eye. My mind is trying to see a head in the bark! Subject: Think you met the challenge well.  Technical: Picture lacks sharpness. As if the focus is off. The leaves need to be more crisp. They look flat. Color is there, but not the plant detail. DOF looks good. This could be as a result of  the ISO:400, or the file size you submitted. Reviewing your file size, I see you didnt take advantage of the 640 max dimension, and your file size was well below the 150k allowed. (624 X 437, 115k) Summary: Nice picture! Good eye and kudos for having your camera handy! I think you captured the theme well. Good burst of color on a grey/black background! Better detail on the green leaves would have helped.', '2006-01-18 10:39:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2053913, 278080, 25571, '<td valign="top">''gratz shin on a very well done picture..<br/> <br/>How did you manage this? what post prod did you do?</td>', '''gratz shin on a very well done picture.. How did you manage this? what post prod did you do?', '2006-01-18 11:37:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2053925, 278227, 25270, '<td valign="top">Many thanks to the Critique Club for their comments---they were very helpful!  Thanks to all who took the time to comment!  Really enjoying the challenges.</td>', 'Many thanks to the Critique Club for their comments---they were very helpful!  Thanks to all who took the time to comment!  Really enjoying the challenges.', '2006-01-18 11:38:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2053970, 278407, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Greetings from Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I initially find this image as underexposed, which in voting would tend to sway my vote low without much other consideration.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>To be perfectly honest, I find the composition and choice of crop boring. Perhaps a less square crop would have brougnt more interest or moving the legs more to one side of the crop.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Subject is clear, it is easy to tell what you were trying to show.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour, focus, and light):</b> <br/>This is what got ya.<br/>Focus: On closer inspection, the image appears to be well focus, but the overall underexposure gives the initial impression that it is softly focused.<br/>Colour: Once again, exposure hurt you on this. What woudld have been vibrant shoes, just went dull.<br/>Light: The source of what went wrong here. I undertand completely that dark skin is hard to expose for. Quite hard indeed. In this case, you should meter from a grey card and then bracket the shot. Other qualities of the light here is that it is quite flat.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Pay more attention to metering of light. Technicals are the first and foremost aspect to work on.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>You seem to have the creative mind to do well. Work on the technicals some and you''ll be on your way to some truly great photos.<br/> <br/>Hope to see more from you soon,<br/>Leroy</td>', '::: Greetings from Critique Club :::  Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission. First Impression - the most important one: I initially find this image as underexposed, which in voting would tend to sway my vote low without much other consideration. Composition: To be perfectly honest, I find the composition and choice of crop boring. Perhaps a less square crop would have brougnt more interest or moving the legs more to one side of the crop. Subject: Subject is clear, it is easy to tell what you were trying to show. Technical (Colour, focus, and light): This is what got ya.Focus: On closer inspection, the image appears to be well focus, but the overall underexposure gives the initial impression that it is softly focused.Colour: Once again, exposure hurt you on this. What woudld have been vibrant shoes, just went dull.Light: The source of what went wrong here. I undertand completely that dark skin is hard to expose for. Quite hard indeed. In this case, you should meter from a grey card and then bracket the shot. Other qualities of the light here is that it is quite flat. To grow its vote?: Pay more attention to metering of light. Technicals are the first and foremost aspect to work on. Summary: You seem to have the creative mind to do well. Work on the technicals some and you''ll be on your way to some truly great photos. Hope to see more from you soon,Leroy', '2006-01-18 11:49:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2053999, 278080, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Greetings from Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Wow, what can I say? Great capture! Would have scored high with me. Very vibrant and very well exposed.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Works well. To be a bit nit-picky I''d like to see the flower just a tad more to the right, but hey, the composition definitel worked for ya.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Subject is very strong... nothing can be improved here.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour, focus, and light):</b> <br/>ALL GOOD! And VERY NICE LIGHTING!<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>LOL, can''t exactly tell ya how to grow the vote much past a blue ribbon. Just keep up the stunning work.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Keep up this kind of work and you''ll be seeing more ribbons in your future!<br/> <br/>Hope to see more from you soon,<br/>Leroy</td>', '::: Greetings from Critique Club :::  Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission. First Impression - the most important one: Wow, what can I say? Great capture! Would have scored high with me. Very vibrant and very well exposed. Composition: Works well. To be a bit nit-picky I''d like to see the flower just a tad more to the right, but hey, the composition definitel worked for ya. Subject: Subject is very strong... nothing can be improved here. Technical (Colour, focus, and light): ALL GOOD! And VERY NICE LIGHTING! To grow its vote?: LOL, can''t exactly tell ya how to grow the vote much past a blue ribbon. Just keep up the stunning work. Summary: Keep up this kind of work and you''ll be seeing more ribbons in your future! Hope to see more from you soon,Leroy', '2006-01-18 11:56:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054001, 278577, 51308, '<td valign="top">very nice</td>', 'very nice', '2006-01-18 11:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054035, 278422, 49672, '<td valign="top">Ha!  This is great!  Did you and Bazz conspire for this challenge?</td>', 'Ha!  This is great!  Did you and Bazz conspire for this challenge?', '2006-01-18 12:09:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054086, 278597, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Greetings from Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Wow, look at the pretty colors. Definitely that is my firs timpression.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Composition isn''t the strongest part of this photo, but it''s acceptible.  Putting a bit more black space to the right side of the photo would have made the "Burst of Color" more interesting.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Subject is clear and well executed.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour, focus, and light):</b> <br/>All good! Colour is vibrant and well-saturated. Focus is sharp and shows great detail. Light is just right and well exposed.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Somehow get some water droplets into play? LOL ... seriously, you made a wonderful caputre here. Perhaps a little more interest in the composition would have grown the vote a bit.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Job well done! You definitely had a good run here. <br/> <br/>Hope to see more from you soon,<br/>Leroy</td>', '::: Greetings from Critique Club :::  Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission. First Impression - the most important one: Wow, look at the pretty colors. Definitely that is my firs timpression. Composition: Composition isn''t the strongest part of this photo, but it''s acceptible.  Putting a bit more black space to the right side of the photo would have made the "Burst of Color" more interesting. Subject: Subject is clear and well executed. Technical (Colour, focus, and light): All good! Colour is vibrant and well-saturated. Focus is sharp and shows great detail. Light is just right and well exposed. To grow its vote?: Somehow get some water droplets into play? LOL ... seriously, you made a wonderful caputre here. Perhaps a little more interest in the composition would have grown the vote a bit. Summary: Job well done! You definitely had a good run here.  Hope to see more from you soon,Leroy', '2006-01-18 12:23:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054105, 278422, 51303, '<td valign="top">so cute..the colors and the eyes awesome</td>', 'so cute..the colors and the eyes awesome', '2006-01-18 12:26:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054170, 277862, 32321, '<td valign="top">Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>First Impression: Nice color, lots of colortoo much color. Eyes are drawn to the green ring and then orange, red and blue. <br/> <br/>Composition: Given the vivid colors, the image is a little busy. Two rings with a center may have been more effective. In this case less may have been better.<br/> <br/>Subject: Think you met the challenge, definitely a burst of color!<br/> <br/>Technical: Very good colors, very vivid. Nice lighting. Excellent focus. Sharp detail. Material kisses are sitting on has some distracting colors. Outside the blue ring, there is a blue tone. As you go inside the blue ring it goes much whiter, and material texture is more prominent. Texture is due to DOF, not sure why there was a color shift.<br/> <br/>Suggestions: As this was a studio shot Try with fewer rings. See if there is more impact, or take a wider shot. Dont crop so close <br/> <br/>Summary: Nice picture, lots of color with sharp detail. <br/></td>', 'Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club. First Impression: Nice color, lots of colortoo much color. Eyes are drawn to the green ring and then orange, red and blue.  Composition: Given the vivid colors, the image is a little busy. Two rings with a center may have been more effective. In this case less may have been better. Subject: Think you met the challenge, definitely a burst of color! Technical: Very good colors, very vivid. Nice lighting. Excellent focus. Sharp detail. Material kisses are sitting on has some distracting colors. Outside the blue ring, there is a blue tone. As you go inside the blue ring it goes much whiter, and material texture is more prominent. Texture is due to DOF, not sure why there was a color shift. Suggestions: As this was a studio shot Try with fewer rings. See if there is more impact, or take a wider shot. Dont crop so close  Summary: Nice picture, lots of color with sharp detail. ', '2006-01-18 12:39:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054336, 278422, 93, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by carpents:</b></div><hr/><i> Ha!  This is great!  Did you and Bazz conspire for this challenge? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hahaha.. no, not at all, but we certainly recognize the children we use in our photos. lol.  (Having used them so often in challenges)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by carpents: Ha!  This is great!  Did you and Bazz conspire for this challenge?   hahaha.. no, not at all, but we certainly recognize the children we use in our photos. lol.  (Having used them so often in challenges)', '2006-01-18 13:23:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054338, 278340, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First off, I must tell you I loved your "Food" entry.  Right, don''t need rocket science, just need good ideas and execution.<br/> <br/>Okay, back to the subject at hand.  Your kiwi abstract.  I like the composition very much.  The star shape in the center and the black seeds around it make a lovely pattern.  And of course the gradiations of green are lovely.<br/> <br/>Unfortunately, even though it is an abstract, usually people like something to be sharp.  And it''s likely that the overall soft-focus of this image worked against you in this Challenge.<br/> <br/>You are doing well after only four Challenges, and I wish you well in future competitions.  Welcome aboard.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  First off, I must tell you I loved your "Food" entry.  Right, don''t need rocket science, just need good ideas and execution. Okay, back to the subject at hand.  Your kiwi abstract.  I like the composition very much.  The star shape in the center and the black seeds around it make a lovely pattern.  And of course the gradiations of green are lovely. Unfortunately, even though it is an abstract, usually people like something to be sharp.  And it''s likely that the overall soft-focus of this image worked against you in this Challenge. You are doing well after only four Challenges, and I wish you well in future competitions.  Welcome aboard.', '2006-01-18 13:23:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054377, 277610, 41701, '<td valign="top">Wow!  Really nice work.</td>', 'Wow!  Really nice work.', '2006-01-18 13:34:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054584, 275651, 47117, '<td valign="top">Thank you sdunsmoor!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thank you sdunsmoor! ', '2006-01-18 14:44:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2054881, 278598, 40370, '<td valign="top">Excellent finish, I''ve never been a fan of eye images but your entry is making me realize I am missing out on a fabulous subject of photograghy... look forward to meeting you on the Southern Utah GTG in May.</td>', 'Excellent finish, I''ve never been a fan of eye images but your entry is making me realize I am missing out on a fabulous subject of photograghy... look forward to meeting you on the Southern Utah GTG in May.', '2006-01-18 15:51:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2055046, 278525, 24454, '<td valign="top">Laurie, this is AWESOME!  My mom has a cat that looks exactly like this.  She is 17, almost 18 years old!!!  In fact, she outlived my mom.  Its a great, colorful photo!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Laurie, this is AWESOME!  My mom has a cat that looks exactly like this.  She is 17, almost 18 years old!!!  In fact, she outlived my mom.  Its a great, colorful photo! ', '2006-01-18 16:35:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2055211, 278134, 21714, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by IceRock:</b></div><hr/><i> to dark background specially because this is spouse to be a photo-picture </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Of course :S</td>', 'Originally posted by IceRock: to dark background specially because this is spouse to be a photo-picture   Of course :S', '2006-01-18 17:11:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2055757, 277549, 42013, '<td valign="top">Hi from the CC<br/> <br/>First impression: The sharpness and color of the front ball is impressive.  The title takes a second but is a clever touch. Back ball seems a little to out of focus and my eyes keep wandering back to it and trying to connect it to the jade.<br/> <br/>Composition: Good crop which accentuates the relationship between the two balls.  I would suggest a little more white space around the jade ball, especially to the left.  I also feel the two shapes would have worked more strongly if the blue ball was moved a little to the left in your frame as well.  I would like to see the blue ball just a bit more in focus.<br/> <br/>Color and lighting: Great color, good white balance and I like the shadows cast by your lighting.  More diffusion of the light to minimize reflections on the jade would have enhanced image IMO.<br/> <br/>Challenge: both stones look like they have wonderful color and detail.  I think either one would have worked well as a focal point.  You met the challenge well and good luck on your next one.</td>', 'Hi from the CC First impression: The sharpness and color of the front ball is impressive.  The title takes a second but is a clever touch. Back ball seems a little to out of focus and my eyes keep wandering back to it and trying to connect it to the jade. Composition: Good crop which accentuates the relationship between the two balls.  I would suggest a little more white space around the jade ball, especially to the left.  I also feel the two shapes would have worked more strongly if the blue ball was moved a little to the left in your frame as well.  I would like to see the blue ball just a bit more in focus. Color and lighting: Great color, good white balance and I like the shadows cast by your lighting.  More diffusion of the light to minimize reflections on the jade would have enhanced image IMO. Challenge: both stones look like they have wonderful color and detail.  I think either one would have worked well as a focal point.  You met the challenge well and good luck on your next one.', '2006-01-18 19:24:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2055810, 278148, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Pascal! What do you know.  I''ve drawn another of your images for a critique.  <br/> <br/>Well, this time you''re not running off the edge of the earth into a blazing sun, you''re looking for a Rainbow.  It''s a great idea, but execution may have been a problem for you.<br/> <br/>It seems to me that there is quite a bit of information in this image and you might want to remove some of it to make the center of attraction more obvious and important.  For example, that white space in the top left, is the brightest thing in the image and it draws the attention of the viewer - not what you want to have happen. And it adds little to the ''Burst of Color'' theme.<br/> <br/>I''d suggest cropping down quite a bit, still leaving some of the horizontal bars in the frame (to avoid the dreaded copying another person''s art work rule) and perhaps cropping into the colored arc just a bit as well.<br/> <br/>Finally, Pascal, I''d suggest using a tripod for this type of image.  It is just a tiny bit soft, and you might think about how it would look tack-sharp.<br/> <br/>Okay, that''ll give you something to go on, and I''m delighted to see that you are enjoying DPC.  Keep up the good work.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Pascal! What do you know.  I''ve drawn another of your images for a critique.   Well, this time you''re not running off the edge of the earth into a blazing sun, you''re looking for a Rainbow.  It''s a great idea, but execution may have been a problem for you. It seems to me that there is quite a bit of information in this image and you might want to remove some of it to make the center of attraction more obvious and important.  For example, that white space in the top left, is the brightest thing in the image and it draws the attention of the viewer - not what you want to have happen. And it adds little to the ''Burst of Color'' theme. I''d suggest cropping down quite a bit, still leaving some of the horizontal bars in the frame (to avoid the dreaded copying another person''s art work rule) and perhaps cropping into the colored arc just a bit as well. Finally, Pascal, I''d suggest using a tripod for this type of image.  It is just a tiny bit soft, and you might think about how it would look tack-sharp. Okay, that''ll give you something to go on, and I''m delighted to see that you are enjoying DPC.  Keep up the good work.', '2006-01-18 19:37:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2055826, 275651, 42013, '<td valign="top">After more review I feel that this shot was slightly underrated. voted 7 personally and i''m not sure why I didnt''t make it an 8 or 9.<br/>mark</td>', 'After more review I feel that this shot was slightly underrated. voted 7 personally and i''m not sure why I didnt''t make it an 8 or 9.mark', '2006-01-18 19:39:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2056578, 278363, 31818, '<td valign="top">I want to thank everyone for their comments.  I agree with most and next time I will concentrate more on the focus.  I think that the focus may have moved this to a top 25 finisher.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I want to thank everyone for their comments.  I agree with most and next time I will concentrate more on the focus.  I think that the focus may have moved this to a top 25 finisher. ', '2006-01-18 22:23:00.000000', NULL, 0),
