(2071304, 277772, 38865, '<td valign="top">new layer, adjust levels to make image almost invisible for the black, change opacity to bring image back through, followed by a paint brush to bring details through on a masked layer</td>', 'new layer, adjust levels to make image almost invisible for the black, change opacity to bring image back through, followed by a paint brush to bring details through on a masked layer', '2006-01-22 15:29:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2071493, 277610, 17507, '<td valign="top">fabulous photo - great from the exposure through the editing. Thanks for posting the original - I think it''s really valuable for many of us. I hope to someday have processing skills at your level.</td>', 'fabulous photo - great from the exposure through the editing. Thanks for posting the original - I think it''s really valuable for many of us. I hope to someday have processing skills at your level.', '2006-01-22 16:23:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2071710, 276321, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>One of the fun things about this critique Club job is the opportunity to wander through portfolios that I might miss otherwise.  Your architecture section is fascinating.  Really a delight.<br/> <br/>Okay, back to work.  You''ve presented a half &amp; half image, indeed.  It meets the challenge, but didn''t score very well.  Sometimes, with images divided essentially in half, the viewer just doesn''t know where to look to find the point of interest, gives up and moves on.  Perhaps this is what happened here.  There are nice textures in the red - although they need time to be studied - and the rocks also have some interest.  <br/> <br/>My suggestion, since your portfolio also tells me you like earth tones, is to think about introducing a third color, such as yellow ochre into the composition.  This might give it some zing and keep the viewer in the picture long enough to enjoy it. <br/> <br/>I wish you much success in your adventures here at DPChallenge.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  One of the fun things about this critique Club job is the opportunity to wander through portfolios that I might miss otherwise.  Your architecture section is fascinating.  Really a delight. Okay, back to work.  You''ve presented a half & half image, indeed.  It meets the challenge, but didn''t score very well.  Sometimes, with images divided essentially in half, the viewer just doesn''t know where to look to find the point of interest, gives up and moves on.  Perhaps this is what happened here.  There are nice textures in the red - although they need time to be studied - and the rocks also have some interest.   My suggestion, since your portfolio also tells me you like earth tones, is to think about introducing a third color, such as yellow ochre into the composition.  This might give it some zing and keep the viewer in the picture long enough to enjoy it.  I wish you much success in your adventures here at DPChallenge. Alice', '2006-01-22 17:40:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2072002, 277888, 43434, '<td valign="top">critique to follow<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-22 19:54:13.</i></td>', 'critique to follow', '2006-01-22 19:52:53.000000', '2006-01-22 19:54:13.000000', 0),
(2072004, 277888, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>The critique I am doing is for "Macaw"<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>This is a good picture, I wish there was more to the background that could have framed the bird.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Not bad with an interesting DOF ... There seems to be some distortion where it looks like two layers met around the bird where some editing has taken place (I may be wrong but that is what it looked like).<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>I do like the colours ... and meets the challenge well.   I would have liked to have seen the real background colour ... or a little more of it ... as the dark just seems a little unreal.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Nicely lit with reasonably good bold use of colour.  <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Well done, I think that taking note of the comments received ... which is funny as some say good focus and others say not focused, but try to look at the picture from others perspectives will allow you to grow scores and also see what others are seeing.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>I think this is a good picture, weel executed with only minor if any issues .. not one of your best scoring, but you have done ok.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. The critique I am doing is for "Macaw" First Impression - the most important one: This is a good picture, I wish there was more to the background that could have framed the bird. Composition: Not bad with an interesting DOF ... There seems to be some distortion where it looks like two layers met around the bird where some editing has taken place (I may be wrong but that is what it looked like). Subject: I do like the colours ... and meets the challenge well.   I would have liked to have seen the real background colour ... or a little more of it ... as the dark just seems a little unreal. Technical (Colour and light): Nicely lit with reasonably good bold use of colour.   To grow its vote?: Well done, I think that taking note of the comments received ... which is funny as some say good focus and others say not focused, but try to look at the picture from others perspectives will allow you to grow scores and also see what others are seeing. Summary: I think this is a good picture, weel executed with only minor if any issues .. not one of your best scoring, but you have done ok. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-01-22 19:54:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2072047, 277038, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>The critique I am doing is for "the magic of wishes"<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I love it ... it took my breath away and left me wishing for more.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Interesting use of composition.   I would loved to have had more details about what you were <br/> <br/>trying to achieve with the shot, as it helps with critiquing.  Apart from that, the comments you <br/> <br/>recieved are positive with a couple to note:<br/> <br/>Careful with neat image, it takes away to texture if used too heavily.<br/>Good concept and great idea!<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>I like the colours ... and how you have used them to meet the challenge 100%..<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Well lit with good bold use of colour.  <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Probably a little much in the neat image.  but I really think an awesome shot .. and defiantely <br/> <br/>was in with a chance .. I just can''t figure out the one and two.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>I think this is a cool picture, well executed with only minor if any issues .. you really did do <br/> <br/>good..<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. The critique I am doing is for "the magic of wishes" First Impression - the most important one: I love it ... it took my breath away and left me wishing for more. Composition: Interesting use of composition.   I would loved to have had more details about what you were  trying to achieve with the shot, as it helps with critiquing.  Apart from that, the comments you  recieved are positive with a couple to note: Careful with neat image, it takes away to texture if used too heavily.Good concept and great idea! Subject: I like the colours ... and how you have used them to meet the challenge 100%.. Technical (Colour and light): Well lit with good bold use of colour.   To grow its vote?: Probably a little much in the neat image.  but I really think an awesome shot .. and defiantely  was in with a chance .. I just can''t figure out the one and two. Summary: I think this is a cool picture, well executed with only minor if any issues .. you really did do  good.. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-01-22 20:10:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2072087, 278196, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>The critique I am doing is for "Welcome home"<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Vibrant, but slightly overtaken by the white background as the tips of the flowers blended in.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I really like this composition, the use of vertical thirds works, although I would have liked to see the stamen on the horizontal thirds to see if that would have added an extra dimension.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>I like the colours ... the background colour was however a minor issue, I feel that the stark white detracted from the image which started to blend with it.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Well lit with good use of colour.  <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>I would think about the cropping used and try looking at the leading lines and thirds rule.  Think about how to make the image pop with different uses of background colour.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Fantastic picture which in reality did VERY well and voted well,  You did a great job.  And good to have this as a learning expereince with the the softbox concept.  YOU SHOULD BE PROUD!<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. The critique I am doing is for "Welcome home" First Impression - the most important one: Vibrant, but slightly overtaken by the white background as the tips of the flowers blended in. Composition: I really like this composition, the use of vertical thirds works, although I would have liked to see the stamen on the horizontal thirds to see if that would have added an extra dimension. Subject: I like the colours ... the background colour was however a minor issue, I feel that the stark white detracted from the image which started to blend with it. Technical (Colour and light): Well lit with good use of colour.   To grow its vote?: I would think about the cropping used and try looking at the leading lines and thirds rule.  Think about how to make the image pop with different uses of background colour. Summary: Fantastic picture which in reality did VERY well and voted well,  You did a great job.  And good to have this as a learning expereince with the the softbox concept.  YOU SHOULD BE PROUD! If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-01-22 20:25:13.000000', NULL, 0),
