(2078059, 278408, 16912, '<td valign="top">Coming from the 1-4-0 thread,<br/> <br/>I''m a lover of negative space, this has plenty :) for me, the ''poofy'' scarf could be sharper and it looks like you over corrected the exposure in the RAW converter to get the bg pure white?<br/> <br/>I do like the idea and look forward to seeing version 2 ;)</td>', 'Coming from the 1-4-0 thread, I''m a lover of negative space, this has plenty :) for me, the ''poofy'' scarf could be sharper and it looks like you over corrected the exposure in the RAW converter to get the bg pure white? I do like the idea and look forward to seeing version 2 ;)', '2006-01-24 13:18:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2085138, 277188, 32133, '<td valign="top">That shot is beautiful!</td>', 'That shot is beautiful!', '2006-01-25 22:26:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2087997, 276601, 42792, '<td valign="top">Hi June, just realized I didn''t leave you a comment on this before.  I really liked the creative composition and idea here.  One of the most original.  Gave it a 7.  I would have voted it higher if there didn''t seem to be a lot of confusion as to what to focus on.  For one, I think the red "burst" should have been in better focus as it''s part of the main picture elements.  I think the spotted background could be interesting if it was more evenly covered.  Not sure the gaussien blur helped.  And where there are spots that show up through the red ... would have been better to clone them out IMO.</td>', 'Hi June, just realized I didn''t leave you a comment on this before.  I really liked the creative composition and idea here.  One of the most original.  Gave it a 7.  I would have voted it higher if there didn''t seem to be a lot of confusion as to what to focus on.  For one, I think the red "burst" should have been in better focus as it''s part of the main picture elements.  I think the spotted background could be interesting if it was more evenly covered.  Not sure the gaussien blur helped.  And where there are spots that show up through the red ... would have been better to clone them out IMO.', '2006-01-26 12:23:58.000000', NULL, 0),
